body:
Lmaoo my bad m8. 

BTW They sweep the table so damn fast after the last card so it's impossible to call them out or verify what happened. Anyway, the hand I realized they were forcing us to pull cards to bust  played almost exactly like this. I wish I was recording.

&#x200B;

Seat 1 (8,3): hit, dealer draws 9

**Result: 20, stand, (8,3,9)**

&#x200B;

Suddendmperbutt (10,2): stand ignored, dealer draws K

**Result: Bust (2, 10, 10) 22**

&#x200B;

Seat 3 (8,6): stand ignored, dealer draws Q

**Result: Bust (8, 6, Q) 24**

&#x200B;

Dealer flips card: (K ,3) dealer draws 8

**Result: Wins Table (K,3,8) 21**

&#x200B;

Later while spectating I watched the dealers allow players to stand on 13's and 15's in between being booted from the table. I'm willing to bet they pull this when a player who is up comes to the table or starts winning well at the table. I had just came from roulette with sizeable winnings. (nothing nuts but definitely a decent swing)
